# Generated by `build switches` from src/sh/tools.inc. Do not edit:
# the kit lane fails when this file and its sources disagree.

config MOONWATER_TOOLS_ALL
    bool "Build every tool unless it is switched off below"
    depends on MOONWATER_CORE=y
    default y
    help
      The default of every MOONWATER_TOOL_ switch. Leave it on and
      switch single tools off; turn it off and switch on the ones
      to keep, which is how kernel/profile/sec_locked is an allow
      list. A tool switched off is compiled out of the shell's
      table and linked nowhere, so its name is not found.

      /init, /term and /moonwater have no switch: the kernel and
      init run them by path, and an image without one does not
      boot.

menu "Tools: general utilities"
    depends on MOONWATER_UTILITIES

